    "body": "Or if it helps, when you embed an XHTML document via an `iframe` that document doesn't become exempt from the xhtml content document rules, so there's no reason why referencing SVGs from `img` or `object` would require a different definition of SVG.\r\n\r\nThe only unique case is when an `svg` element is directly embedded in the HTML. The restrictions need to be the same as standalone SVGs, but the vocabulary stuff is already handled by the HTML requirements (e.g., the `prefix` attribute should only be on the root `html` element, while `epub:type` is still allowed anywhere).",
